# Local H2 database (local profile)
# Anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, this matched a directory named `data` at
# any depth - which since the client moved in here includes
# client/composeApp/src/.../core/data, the package holding every repository in the app.
# Files already tracked kept working, so the only symptom was that *new* ones silently
# refused to be committed.
/data/
*.mv.db
*.trace.db

# The frontend build lands on the jar's classpath via target/, never here. Kept ignored
# because older builds unpacked bundles into this directory, and a stale copy left in a
# working tree must not be committed.
/src/main/resources/static/

# Self-hosted compose state (docker-compose.yml bind mounts).
/postgres/
